# Nothing is declared in these files. What is expected of a place is what the text writes into it: of the parameter `table` the record of the literal that the one call written in the function's own file hands over;
# of the fields `handler` and `bias` the arrow and the number that the literals written in the files in sight of the reader lay there; of the constant `kept` the record that its own file stores into it.
# All of it is only expected: each is tested, here in front of the loops. A file that the reader's text does not name says nothing: stranger.js hands over a text under `bias` and another arrow, and run() is compiled as without it.
# Where one of the values written is not told by its own text (`globalThis.seen.length`), nothing is said of the place.
# TODO: what the file of a function says: the guess here rested on what the whole program was seen to hand over, store or return; it comes back with what the calls and stores written in the function's own file say
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: b0(v0: L1?{{*}}
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=f7
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=i32
# CHECK: Add {{*}} form=Integers
# CHECK: ToInt32
# RUN(KEPT): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# KEPT: ShapeTest {{*}} layouts=[L2]
# KEPT: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=f6
